    "finalText": "**Everything works now.** Amabie verified the candidate from outside the tree, promoted it (`main` fast-forwarded `6f2924d → 92898fa`), and the post-proof confirmed the promoted base bytes are byte-identical to the verified tree. Both suites pass on the base: `node run-tests.js` → 44 passing, `node checks/contract.cjs` → passed.\n\n## What was broken and what I changed\n\n**`src/storage.js` — tenant isolation.** `key()` returned the bare `id`, so equal ids in different tenants collided. Now `JSON.stringify([tenant, id])` — injective for all strings, so punctuation/delimiter combinations (`a|b`+`c` vs `a`+`b|c`, quotes/brackets) cannot collide either.\n\n**`src/replay.js` — replay lost deletions.** `replay` filtered to `op === 'put'`, so `open(exportJournal())` silently dropped deletes. Now applies every event in order.\n\n**`src/api.js` — stale reads and a rogue batch path.**\n- `apply()` never invalidated the cache, so cached hits *and* cached misses went stale after `put`/`remove`. `apply()` now evicts the key from the cache.\n- `batch` bypassed `apply()` entirely: it applied delete events as puts and skipped cache invalidation. All three mutation entry points (`put`, `remove`, `batch`) now route through the same `mutate → apply` path, in call order.\n\n**`run-tests.js` — added coverage.** The smoke test was expanded to 44 assertions covering: cross-tenant independence, delimiter/punctuation key collisions, freshness after every mutation path (for both cached hits and misses), batch call ordering, export detachment (mutating the returned array or its events changes nothing), replay including deletions, repeated-replay equivalence, full history preserved across replay and subsequent mutations, and that the `open(history)` input array is copied. I mutation-checked it: reverting any one of the three fixes alone makes both suites fail.\n\nThe API surface (`open/put/remove/batch/get/exportJournal`) and `docs/CONTRACT.md` were left unchanged; checks were strengthened, not weakened. The candidate worktree and its evidence record remain in place — say the word if you want `amabie isolate --remove repair-tenant-ledger` cleanup run."
  },
